# Documentation rules

- README, `llms.txt`, `index.d.ts`, the /docs page and `docs/*.md` must agree. API facts come from `src/index.js`
  and `index.d.ts`; check them there before writing.
- README `## Recipes` is rendered verbatim into /docs framework tabs (`site/partials/docs-frameworks.mjs`). Each recipe
  is a `**Title**` line followed by a fenced block. Tabs match recipes by title prefix (`ORDER` in that file), and the
  build throws if a recipe has no tab or a tab has no recipe, so add/rename both together.
- Keep the honesty note: React 19, Vue 3.5, Svelte 5 and React SSR were actually run; Next.js, Nuxt, SvelteKit, Astro,
  Angular and WordPress recipes follow official docs but **haven't been run**. Don't upgrade a claim without running it.
- Sizes are gzip -9 of `dist/*.js` (`npm run size`). Update every mention (README, llms.txt, PROJECT-GOALS, AGENTS.md)
  when they change. Browser-support claims need a source and a date (see `docs/ROADMAP.md`).
- The production domain isn't decided; `https://ghost-reveal.vercel.app` is a placeholder. Don't link to it as live.
- The project's previous names appear only in the name history (`docs/PROJECT-GOALS.md` §3). Never reintroduce them, including in variable names.
- Record new decisions in `docs/PROJECT-GOALS.md` (§9 decisions, §14 decisions log, §10 open questions).
- Plain language, short paragraphs, no em-dash-heavy marketing copy.
